(A learner who reads a page a day will finish a short novel in a season.) Tj T*
(The trick is not the volume of the text but the regularity of the habit.) Tj T*
(Ten minutes every morning beat three hours once a month, because a language) Tj T*
(is a set of reflexes and reflexes are built by repetition, not by effort.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(When you meet an unknown word, read the whole sentence again before you) Tj T*
(reach for a dictionary. Most of the time the sentence already tells you) Tj T*
(what the word means, and a meaning you reconstructed yourself is much) Tj T*
(harder to forget than a meaning somebody handed to you.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Speaking is the part that people postpone the longest. It helps to start) Tj T*
(with texts you have already read: retell one paragraph out loud, slowly,) Tj T*
(and do not stop to correct yourself in the middle of a sentence. Correct) Tj T*
(the sentence after you finish it, and then say the whole thing once more.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(At the end of the week, look back at what you read. Pick the five words) Tj T*
